@anon.9efbc0c128adab6190fabe7f7e045142.518 = private unnamed_addr constant <{ [919 x i8] }> <{ [919 x i8] c"Separates a region into multiple equally sized columns.\0A\0AThe `column` function allows to separate the interior of any container into\0Amultiple columns. It will not equalize the height of the columns, instead,\0Athe columns will take up the height of their container or the remaining\0Aheight on the page. The columns function can break across pages if\0Anecessary.\0A\0AIf you need to insert columns across your whole document, you can use the\0A[`{page}` function's `columns` parameter]($page.columns) instead.\0A\0A# Example\0A```example\0A= Towards Advanced Deep Learning\0A\0A#box(height: 68pt,\0A columns(2, gutter: 11pt)[\0A   #set par(justify: true)\0A   This research was funded by the\0A   National Academy of Sciences.\0A   NAoS provided support for field\0A   tests and interviews with a\0A   grant of up to USD 40.000 for a\0A   period of 6 months.\0A ]\0A)\0A\0AIn recent years, deep learning has\0Aincreasingly been used to solve a\0Avariety of problems.\0A```" }>, align 1
